${w}_i$\end{document} are initialised to 1.0 and are optimized during training. These projectors let the biochemical constraints affects differently in the 8-dimensional latent space, with the learnable weights controlling the strength of the effect and the projectors determining which combination of latent dimensions are modulated by a given constraint. The quantitative results of per-constraint shift on different dimensions are presented in the Supplementary Table 2. The 8-dimensional latent space in CVAE model is not intended to correspond directly to individual biochemical features (e.g. a ‘charge’ or ‘hydrophobicity’ dimension). Instead, the encoder learns a distributed, continuous representation of peptide sequences that supports accurate reconstruction, while biochemical properties (MIC ≤ 10 μg/mL, net charge, length, instability index, Boman index) are incorporated via separate conditional projector networks operating on dedicated label streams.
